<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/7th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Moira</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/637">637</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> · Also known as Battle of Mag Rath</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Moira, Mag Rath in Irish, was fought in 637 near Moira in County Down. The high king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/domnall-mac-aedo">Domnall mac Áedo</a> of the Northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ui-neill">Uí Néill</a> defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congal-caech">Congal Cáech</a>, king of the Dál nAraidi, and his ally <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/domnall-brecc">Domnall Brecc</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dal-riata">Dál Riata</a>; Congal was killed. The battle ended Ulaid hopes of the high kingship and weakened Dál Riata's hold on its lands in Ireland.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Domnall Brecc joined Congal Cáech of the Ulaid in his war against the Irish high king and was defeated at the <b>Battle of Mag Rath</b> in 637, which weakened Dál Riata’s position in Ireland; he was killed fighting the Britons of Strathclyde at Strathcarron in 642.</blockquote><a href="/empire/dal-riata">Dal Riata · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>Defeat at <b>Mag Rath</b> in 637 under Domnall Brecc, and later Pictish conquest, eroded its standing.</blockquote><a href="/state/cenel-ngabrain">Cenel nGabrain</a></li><li><blockquote>Congal Cáech, king of the Ulaid and briefly claimant to the kingship of Tara, allied with Dál Riata but was defeated and killed by Domnall mac Áedo at <b>Mag Rath</b> in 637.</blockquote><a href="/state/dal-naraidi">Dal nAraidi</a></li><li><blockquote>Kings such as Báetán mac Cairill and Congal Cáech challenged the Uí Néill, but defeat at <b>Mag Rath</b> in 637 ended their hopes of wider supremacy.</blockquote><a href="/state/kingdom-of-ulaid">Kingdom of Ulaid</a></li></ul></section>
